me><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byams pa mgon po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreyanātha</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6118</idno><idno type="APIS">3747</idno><note type="comment">Future Buddha held as the author of the works that come to be designated as the "Five Jewels of Maitreya" (ID:6167).</note></person><person xml:id="person3756"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">asaṅga</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon thogs med</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">thogs myed</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6117</idno><idno type="APIS">3756</idno></person><person xml:id="person3786"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog blo ldan shes rab</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྔོག་བློ་ལྡན་ཤེས་རབ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog lo tsA ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo chen</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge slong blo ldan shes rab</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog lo rtsa ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog dge slong blo ldan shes rab</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">blo ldan bzang po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo tsha ba chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo ts+tsha ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo tsha ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo tsa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">blo ldan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ma hA</persName><birth notBefore="1059-01-01" notAfter="1059-12-31">1059</birth><death notBefore="1109-01-01" notAfter="1109-12-31">1109</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2551</idno><idno type="APIS">3786</idno><note type="comment">See [BAQ9MH4T]: 193 for the main events of his life.&#13;
&#13;
Three manuscript editions of his writings and translations were deposited respectively in rNgog Blo ldan shes rab's tomb, in the monastery of gSang phu (probably in the main assembly hall), and in Drin las kyi sde (ID:4357) ([7FZ3B926]: 107).</note></person><person xml:id="person3807"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bre shes rab 'bar</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འབྲེ་ཤེས་རབ་འབར</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bre chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'dre chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'dre shes rab 'bar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bri shes rab 'bar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shes rab bla ma</persName><birth notBefore="1040-01-01" notAfter="1100-12-31">after 1040 before 1100</birth><death notAfter="1200-12-31">before 1200</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2274</idno><idno type="APIS">3807</idno><note type="comment">Further holy places associated to him are: Ze thang, Grwa thang and rMog po ([647FFPZR]: 545, based on [Q3KCZX7B]: 38).&#13;
Remembered for thirteen distinguished objects (such as royal insignia and religious articles), which could be objects of his clan ([4LDAV8UH]: 95.).</note></person><person xml:id="person3893"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam dbyangs 'od zer mgon po</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འཇམ་དབྱངས་འོད་ཟེར་མགོན་པོ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sgros snying pa 'od zer mgon po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sgros rnying pa 'od zer mgon po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa 'od zer mgon po</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01">after 1200</birth><death notAfter="1350-12-31">before 1350</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P8LS14991</idno><idno type="APIS">3893</idno><note type="comment">Seventh abbot of gSang phu lower monastery. [D5VJHLSN]: 19 mentions two 'Od zer mgon po of gSang phu, the abbot, fl. mid-to-late 1200s, and the author of a work on the Perfection of wisdom, fl. late 13th-early 14th c.?.</note></person><person xml:id="person3894"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam dbyangs shakya gzhon nu</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འཇམ་དབྱངས་ཤཀྱ་གཞོན་ནུ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gsang phu shAkya gzhon nu</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gsang phu mkhan po shAkya gzhon nu</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam dbyangs shAkya gzhon nu</persName><birth notAfter="1270-12-31">before 1270</birth><death notBefore="1352-01-01">after 1352</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P5500</idno><idno type="APIS">3894</idno><note type="comment">Eighth throne-holder of gSang phu gling smad and 16th mkhan po of the Gling smad.&#13;
It is reported that during 'Jam dbyang Śākya gzhon nu's time as abbot of the sGros seminary of the Lower monastery (ca. 1326), there was a split between the old (rnying) and the new (gsar). Śākya gzhon nu's oral teachings were taught in "Old sGros" ([7FZ3B926]: 118).&#13;
This, however, conflicts with the dates determined for the dates of activity of the next abbot in [CCSBSVCA]: 686, namely 1293-1301.</note></person><person xml:id="person3895"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">kha rag pa byang chub gzhon nu</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཁ་རག་པ་བྱང་ཆུབ་གཞོན་ནུ</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01" notAfter="1340-12-31">after 1200 before 1340</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">3895</idno><note type="comment">Credited with the creation of a new explanatory style ([8GL7ZT7Y]: 26, translated from [8GL7ZT7Y]: 15a5 (byang gzhon gyi sa bsgros gsar pa brtsams).)</note></person><person xml:id="person4024"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">grags pa rgya mtsho bde legs 'byung gnas</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གྲགས་པ་རྒྱ་མཚོ་བདེ་ལེགས་འབྱུང་གནས</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01">after 1200</birth><death notAfter="1500-12-31">before 1500</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P3JT13458</idno><idno type="APIS">4024</idno><note type="comment">The closing verses mention 'Jam dbyangs 'od zer mgon po (ID:3893) as the source of the teaching - he could be 'Jam dbyangs shakya gzhon nu (ID:3894), the eighth abbot of the Lower monastery of gSang phu and founder of Tshal Gung thang. Possibly, the expression refers to both the eighth abbot ('jam dbyangs) and the seventh ('od zer mngon po).&#13;
See [J4L5X9AG]: 432, n. 58.</note></person><person xml:id="person4593"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">Anonymous</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཨཱནོཉམོཨུས</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4593</idno></person><person xml:id="person5611"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sthirapāla</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bum phrag gsum pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgya gar pan chen</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">jo bo 'bum pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bum</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'bum pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brtan skyong</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dhirapāla</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sthirapāla</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sthirapālaśrībhadra</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">paN+Di ta d+hi ra pA la</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">trilakṣa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bstan skyong</persName><birth notBefore="1050-01-01">after 1050</birth><death notAfter="1150-12-31">before 1150</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4CZ15638</idno><idno type="APIS">5611</idno><note type="comment">Indian paṇḍita. Not to be confused with three Tibetan scholars with the nickname "'Bum phrag gsum pa": (ID:6415), (ID:6416), (ID:6417). See [2X2E3882]: 252, n. 130.</note></person><person xml:id="person5838"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'phags pa blo gros rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འཕགས་པ་བློ་གྲོས་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'phags pa bla ma</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'gro mgon chos rgyal 'phags pa